    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12129" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀπις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιδος</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>, and 
			Ion.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιος</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>Apis,</i> a bull worshipped in
			Egypt, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.153
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> a
			mythical king of Argos, 
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄπιος</span>
			 (B) <i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀπις</span></b> , 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀπία γῆ</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				25.183
			</span></i>, prob. in <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.1564
			</span></i>.</div>
